<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pangeran Santri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pangeran Santri was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumedang">Sumedang</a> Larang in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in the 16th century, under whom the court accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Tradition links him with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirebon">Cirebon</a> sultanate, the main centre of Islam in western Java. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prabu-geusan-ulun">Prabu Geusan Ulun</a> became the kingdom's best-known ruler, expanding it after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> kingdom of Pajajaran.</p></div>
